  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member replying to a topic or an MP, I want to quote a whole message, a selection of it or several messages, so that my answer carries the right `[quotemsg]` blocks.\n\n### Scope\n\nHFRClient (ADR 0008), on top of LOT-048, LOT-031 and the LOT-042 session:\n- **Quote template**: load a message's quote form (LOT-031 quote link) with `PostingFlow.loadForm` (LOT-048) through the selected account's session, and return the server's `content_form` prefill as served. Never rebuild `[quotemsg=…]` (HFR-PROTOCOL: always reuse the server's prefill).\n- **Selection formatter**: a pure port of `ReplyQuoteSelectionFormatter`. One block: its body is replaced by the selection, or the selection is bolded. Several blocks: the first block holding the selection (case-insensitive) is used.\n- **Multi-quote**: the composer GET carries the topic's `quotes…` cookie, kept by the LOT-042 session (`toggleQuote`, `clearQuotes`). After a quoting reply that LOT-048 confirms as `success`, this lot clears that topic's selection: the clean-up the LOT-048 spec leaves to this lot.\n\n- Module: HFRClient · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium\n- Audit source: D4 (`docs/audit/D-posting.md` §2.2)\n- Legacy sources (read-only; francoisgn/hfrnow at `2440d79`, an ancestor of `origin/master`):\n  - `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:36-109` (`ReplyQuoteSelectionFormatter`), `:1852-1945` (multi-quote cookie: name from the `quoter()` arguments, `|<numreponse>` markers, `.hardware.fr`, 1 h, deleted when empty) (at `2440d79`).\n  - `Classes/QuoteMessageViewController.m:459-525` (ObjC selection quote, `[quotemsg]` regex `:469`) (at `2440d79`).\n  - `HFRswift/Swift/ReplyService.swift:767-841` (`fetchQuoteTemplate`, `extractContentForm`), `:902-915` (entity decoding) (at `2440d79`).\n  - `HFRswift/Swift/AccountSessionService.swift:107-115` (`quotes*` cookies kept across the jar reset; not needed with LOT-042's per-account jars) (at `2440d79`).\n  - No legacy code clears the cookie after a post (none found at `2440d79`; it expires after 1 h).\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-049-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-048 (#74, done)\n- LOT-031 (#58, done)\n- Uses the LOT-042 (#68, done) session cookie API.\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged.\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\nReview: this lot writes and deletes a cookie in the account's session (the multi-quote clean-up), so EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md §7 applies: besides your own adversarial review, a review by **another contributor** (`REVIEW WANTED: fable`).\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- With LOT-004 oracles, in `Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Fixtures/captures/`: `R41a` (quote form), `R41b` (quote of a quoting post), `R42` (topic composer with the multi-quote cookie), `R47a` (MP quote form), `R47c` (MP composer with the multi-quote cookie), `W14` (multi-quote reply posted).\n- *Pending capture*: `W14`'s answer sets a cookie named `quoteshardwarefr-prive-<post>` (its meta `set_cookie_names`), but its value and expiry were not recorded, so whether HFR clears the selection itself is unknown (no capture issue yet). The cookie-less multi-quote route is not tested either (HFR-PROTOCOL §7 X10). Never hand-build them (LESSONS 35-36).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Differential test: the prefill returned for `R41a`, `R41b`, `R42`, `R47a` and `R47c` equals the `content_form` of their LOT-004 oracles (CRLF kept as served, entities decoded).\n- [ ] Selection formatter: the legacy cases `HFRswiftTests/ReplyPostingServiceTests.swift:1101-1132` (at `2440d79`) ported, plus selection not found, empty selection and a selection spanning two blocks.\n- [ ] Multi-quote: the composer GET carries exactly that topic's selected markers; after a `success` quoting reply the selection is cleared; on `unconfirmed`, refusal or error the spec states what happens and a test pins it; another topic's selection is untouched.\n- [ ] Quote URLs come only from LOT-031 actions and stay on the forum origin (LESSONS 37, 43); no quote URL is built by hand.\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-049-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n### Old issue (frozen)\n\n[francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#77](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/77) — read-only history.\n",
